# NetworkFeed: Wi-Fi menu. Both looks.
ipc panels open wifiMenu IRICE-TEST
wait 2
shot menu
note Wi-Fi menu opens under the menu bar's Wi-Fi item; with Wi-Fi in the sandbox rows are sorted connected first; without Wi-Fi it shows the same empty/off state as QML.
# NOTE: pointer on the menu keeps rows still; position below is an assumption (menu near the top right)
ptr move 1700 200 sleep 10000
shot hold-still
note After keeping the pointer on the menu for 10 s rows have not reordered; they refresh within 4 s after the pointer leaves (needs networks changing: MANUAL to verify).
# MANUAL: with Wi-Fi hardware: keep pointer on the menu 10 s while networks change: rows hold still; move off -> refresh within 4 s
# MANUAL: toggle the Wi-Fi switch -> list empties / comes back, no crash (needs real hardware; position of the switch from the shot)
ipc panels close
